{"guppy":{"id":"1077fd48-3516-4cc6-ba63-7795903217b0","word":"guppy","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"Poecilia reticulata","word":"guppy"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"Poecilia reticulata","word":"lebiste"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"Poecilia reticulata","word":"barrigudinho"}],"pos":"noun","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"Fred kept a tank of guppies by the windowsill.","bold_text_offsets":[[20,27]],"type":"example","id":"ae9be6dc-a51e-4d0e-a892-73d76d8056bc"}],"head_nr":1,"links":[["Poecilia reticulata","Poecilia reticulata#Translingual"]],"synonyms":[{"word":"millionfish"}],"glosses":["A tiny freshwater fish, Poecilia reticulata, popular in home aquariums, that usually has a plain body and black or dark blue tail for the females and a more colorful tail for the males. The guppies can vary in size, but males are 4 cm (1.6”) and females are 7 cm (2.8”)."],"categories":["English terms with usage examples"],"id":"e92dc9e6-d422-40a8-9c58-b58d1109cc24"},{"examples":[{"text":"Throw that one back; it’s just a guppy!","bold_text_offsets":[[33,38]],"type":"example","id":"1d76f6de-c036-43f8-96b3-73427302822d"}],"head_nr":1,"links":[["tiny","tiny"],["fish","fish"]],"raw_glosses":["(by extension) Any tiny fish."],"glosses":["Any tiny fish."],"categories":["English terms with usage examples"],"tags":["broadly"],"id":"73da0b2c-88e0-42ec-856c-bf1105856e11"},{"examples":[{"text":"I reached into my pack and grabbed a guppy to reload. Pouring in the contents, I kept my eyes ahead as I was supposed to do.","ref":"2001, John R. Little, Curtis Wong, Ultimate Paintball Field Guide, page 177:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[37,42]],"id":"4b9131e5-3029-4598-932b-7fd2768713b4"}],"topics":["games","paintball"],"head_nr":1,"links":[["paintball","paintball"],["tube","tube"],["paintball","paintball"]],"categories":["English terms with quotations","Quotation templates to be clea